   "source": [
    "# HeatSense | Phase 1: Notebook 00 — Dataset Inventory\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective**: Discover and catalog the physical files, directory structure, metadata fields, and basic record layouts of the Phase 1 battery dataset without making unverified assumptions or modifying source files.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Operating Principle**: Read-only inspection. Never overwrite, move, or modify raw dataset files."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1: Environment & Dataset Path Resolution\n",
    "* **Analytical Question**: Where is the dataset physically located on this machine, and can Python access it read-only?\n",
    "* **Why It Matters to HeatSense**: Ensures that the data pipeline connects to the actual data directory without hardcoding rigid machine-specific paths.\n",
    "* **Expected Inputs**: Configurable environment variable `HEATSENSE_DATASET_ROOT` or fallback paths.\n",
    "* **What the Code Does**: Checks `data/raw/cleaned_dataset` inside the repository and `D:/Professional Projects/Digital_twin_project/Datasets/cleaned_dataset` externally, verifying read access.\n",
    "* **Output to Inspect**: Verified dataset root directory path and confirmation of access.\n",
    "* **Decision**: Confirms the active data source directory for all subsequent cells."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check paths in order of priority:\n",
    "candidate_paths = [\n",
    "    Path(os.environ.get(\"HEATSENSE_DATASET_ROOT\", \"\")) if os.environ.get(\"HEATSENSE_DATASET_ROOT\") else None,\n",
    "    Path(\"../../data/raw/cleaned_dataset\"),\n",
    "    Path(\"../data/raw/cleaned_dataset\"),\n",
    "    Path(\"data/raw/cleaned_dataset\"),\n",
    "    Path(\"D:/Professional Projects/Digital_twin_project/Datasets/cleaned_dataset\"),\n",
    "    Path(\"D:/Professional Projects/Digital_twin_project/heatsense-battery-digital-twin/data/raw/cleaned_dataset\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "DATASET_ROOT = None\n",
    "for p in candidate_paths:\n",
    "    if p and p.exists() and (p / \"metadata.csv\").exists():\n",
    "        DATASET_ROOT = p.resolve()\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "if DATASET_ROOT is None:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Dataset root with metadata.csv could not be found. Please set HEATSENSE_DATASET_ROOT.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"[SUCCESS] Active Dataset Root: {DATASET_ROOT}\")\n",
    "print(f\"[CHECK] Exists: {DATASET_ROOT.exists()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2: Top-Level Directory Manifest & Size Audit\n",
    "* **Analytical Question**: What subdirectories and root files exist inside the dataset root, and what are their storage footprints?\n",
    "* **Why It Matters to HeatSense**: Confirms whether expected subfolders (`data/`, `extra_infos/`, `metadata.csv`) are present and intact.\n",
    "* **Expected Inputs**: `DATASET_ROOT` from Cell 1.\n",
    "* **What the Code Does**: Iterates through `DATASET_ROOT`, listing subdirectories, file counts, and sizes in megabytes.\n",
    "* **Output to Inspect**: Table/list of top-level items with file counts and total MB.\n",
    "* **Decision**: Confirms structural completeness of the dataset distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "manifest = []\n",
    "for item in sorted(DATASET_ROOT.iterdir()):\n",
    "    if item.is_dir():\n",
    "        sub_files = list(item.glob(\"*\"))\n",
    "        total_size = sum(f.stat().st_size for f in sub_files if f.is_file()) / (1024 * 1024)\n",
    "        manifest.append({\"Item\": item.name, \"Type\": \"Directory\", \"Count\": len(sub_files), \"Size_MB\": round(total_size, 2)})\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        size_mb = item.stat().st_size / (1024 * 1024)\n",
    "        manifest.append({\"Item\": item.name, \"Type\": \"File\", \"Count\": 1, \"Size_MB\": round(size_mb, 2)})\n",
    "\n",
    "manifest_df = pd.DataFrame(manifest)\n",
    "print(manifest_df.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3: Metadata Schema & Summary Statistics\n",
    "* **Analytical Question**: What does `metadata.csv` contain, what are its columns, row counts, unique battery identifiers, and test types?\n",
    "* **Why It Matters to HeatSense**: `metadata.csv` is the index linking sequential run files (`00001.csv`, etc.) to battery cells, test conditions, temperatures, and measured capacities.\n",
    "* **Expected Inputs**: `metadata.csv` path.\n",
    "* **What the Code Does**: Reads `metadata.csv` using Pandas, checks dimensions, column data types, missing value counts, and lists unique batteries and test types.\n",
    "* **Output to Inspect**: Number of rows, list of columns, table of unique `battery_id` values with test counts, and breakdown of `type`.\n",
    "* **Decision**: Establishes how battery cells are tracked and whether multiple test types (e.g. charge, discharge, impedance) are present."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "meta_path = DATASET_ROOT / \"metadata.csv\"\n",
    "meta_df = pd.read_csv(meta_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Metadata Dimensions: {meta_df.shape[0]} rows x {meta_df.shape[1]} columns\\n\")\n",
    "print(\"Columns and Non-Null Counts:\")\n",
    "print(meta_df.info())\n",
    "print(\"\\nFirst 5 rows of metadata:\")\n",
    "display(meta_df.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nUnique Battery IDs:\", sorted(meta_df['battery_id'].dropna().unique()))\n",
    "print(\"\\nTest Type Breakdown:\")\n",
    "print(meta_df['type'].value_counts())\n",
    "print(\"\\nAmbient Temperature Breakdown (deg C):\")\n",
    "print(meta_df['ambient_temperature'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 4: Extra Infos & Documentation Audit\n",
    "* **Analytical Question**: What documentation files exist in `extra_infos/` and what context do they provide regarding experimental protocols?\n",
    "* **Why It Matters to HeatSense**: README files explain cell chemistry, test equipment, nominal capacity, and cutoff criteria directly from the experimental researchers.\n",
    "* **Expected Inputs**: `extra_infos/` directory.\n",
    "* **What the Code Does**: Lists all files in `extra_infos/` and prints the first 25 lines of a representative README file.\n",
    "* **Output to Inspect**: List of text files and introductory excerpt from one NASA README.\n",
    "* **Decision**: Discloses manufacturer, rated capacity, and cutoff voltage guidelines."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "extra_dir = DATASET_ROOT / \"extra_infos\"\n",
    "if extra_dir.exists():\n",
    "    info_files = sorted(list(extra_dir.glob(\"*\")))\n",
    "    print(f\"Found {len(info_files)} documentation files in extra_infos/:\")\n",
    "    for f in info_files:\n",
    "        print(f\" - {f.name} ({round(f.stat().st_size / 1024, 2)} KB)\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    sample_txt = info_files[0]\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n--- Preview of {sample_txt.name} (first 25 lines) ---\")\n",
    "    with open(sample_txt, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\") as fp:\n",
    "        for _ in range(25):\n",
    "            line = fp.readline()\n",
    "            if not line: break\n",
    "            print(line.rstrip())\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"[WARN] extra_infos directory not found.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 5: Sequential Time-Series Data File Inspection\n",
    "* **Analytical Question**: How are time-series measurements formatted inside the sequential CSVs (e.g., `00001.csv`), and what are the observed sampling intervals?\n",
    "* **Why It Matters to HeatSense**: Confirms exact column headers, numerical precision, sampling frequency ($\Delta t$), and initial signal values.\n",
    "* **Expected Inputs**: `data/00001.csv`.\n",
    "* **What the Code Does**: Loads `00001.csv`, prints summary statistics (`describe()`), computes the distribution of time steps $\\Delta t = t_k - t_{k-1}$, and checks for NaN values.\n",
    "* **Output to Inspect**: Column names, data types, min/max values of voltage/current/temperature, and $\\Delta t$ statistics.\n",
    "* **Decision**: Determines whether sampling is uniform or variable, and verifies sensor signal boundaries."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sample_csv_path = DATASET_ROOT / \"data\" / \"00001.csv\"\n",
    "sample_df = pd.read_csv(sample_csv_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Sample File: {sample_csv_path.name}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Shape: {sample_df.shape[0]} rows x {sample_df.shape[1]} columns\\n\")\n",
    "print(\"Columns:\", list(sample_df.columns))\n",
    "print(\"\\nSummary Statistics:\")\n",
    "display(sample_df.describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute time step delta\n",
    "if \"Time\" in sample_df.columns and len(sample_df) > 1:\n",
    "    dt_series = sample_df[\"Time\"].diff().dropna()\n",
    "    print(\"\\nSampling Interval (dt in seconds) Summary:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Mean dt: {dt_series.mean():.3f}s | Median dt: {dt_series.median():.3f}s | Min dt: {dt_series.min():.3f}s | Max dt: {dt_series.max():.3f}s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 6: Linking Metadata to Sequential Data Files\n",
    "* **Analytical Question**: Does row $i$ in `metadata.csv` match the file referenced in `filename` and correspond to the expected test type and duration?\n",
    "* **Why It Matters to HeatSense**: Validates the indexing integrity of the dataset ingestion pipeline.\n",
    "* **Expected Inputs**: `metadata.csv` row 0 and `00001.csv`.\n",
    "* **What the Code Does**: Retrieves the metadata row for `00001.csv`, prints test type, battery ID, and recorded Capacity, and compares it with the final elapsed time in the data file.\n",
    "* **Output to Inspect**: Consistency check table between metadata and time-series file.\n",
    "* **Decision**: Confirms whether `filename` in `metadata.csv` is the canonical relational key."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "meta_match = meta_df[meta_df[\"filename\"] == \"00001.csv\"]\n",
    "print(\"Metadata record for 00001.csv:\")\n",
    "print(meta_match.to_dict(orient=\"records\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "total_time = sample_df[\"Time\"].max() if \"Time\" in sample_df.columns else None\n",
    "print(f\"\\n00001.csv Record Count: {len(sample_df)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"00001.csv Max Elapsed Time: {total_time:.2f} seconds ({total_time/60:.2f} minutes)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Recorded Metadata Capacity: {meta_match['Capacity'].values[0]} Ah\")"
   ]
  },
  {
